narrative:
Ser Aldous Fenn first entered your life as a pair of polished boots visible beneath a nursery curtain. You were hiding from a lesson on lineage. He did not pretend not to see you.

@Aldous: If you mean to escape, Your Highness, choose a door. Curtains have a poor record in military history.

You expected him to drag you back. Instead, he sat outside the curtain and described every ridiculous ancestor whose portrait hung in the hall, including the queen who accidentally declared war on a duchy because she misread an invitation.

@Aldous: History is a room full of people certain they were being sensible. Remember that before you become one of them.

It was the first time an adult at court made you laugh without asking anything in return.
